      "headline": "Principal Software Engineer · Surgical Robotics & Autonomous Systems · FDA | Published in Science Translational Medicine",
      "about": "I build software for surgical robots that operate on humans.My work spans the full stack of surgical autonomy: computer vision, 3D scene reconstruction, robot control, and FDA-cleared clinical systems. I co-authored the STAR system (Science Translational Medicine, 2016), one of the first demonstrations of supervised autonomous soft tissue surgery, and hold an issued patent on 3D corrected imaging for surgical navigation. At Children's National Medical Center I developed novel CV algorithms for autonomous suturing robots and published in IEEE Transactions on Biomedical Engineering. At Globus Medical I implemented FDA-submitted navigation software for image-guided spinal surgery robots. At Medtronic I've served as Tech Lead across major platform architecture initiatives, driving cross-functional teams of 20+ engineers across three time zones.I presented at the Hamlyn Symposium on Medical Robotics in London and at the Robotics for Good Competition in Dubai.Core expertise: C++, Python, Computer Vision, ROS, OpenCV, Surgical Robotics, FDA Regulatory Software, Autonomous Systems, System Architecture.Most recently, I have served as a technical lead on surgical robotics platform architecture, coordinating 20+ engineers across GUI, embedded controls, state machines, vendors, and distributed teams.I'm always interested in conversations about surgical autonomy, medical robotics, and the intersection of AI and clinical systems.",
